    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "In May 2026, a critical equipment failure at Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2 sparked a grid incident across the Visayas island group, forcing the power network manager to initiate a system-wide power alert. This emergency response, combined with prolonged plant failures from other facilities, created a severe energy deficit of over 950 megawatts, compelling authorities to order emergency load shedding to stabilize the grid.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Creator",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Following a generator system failure, the electricity grid controller was compelled to unleash a grid crisis protocol in the Philippines region, implementing controlled power curtailment to prevent a major transmission overload. The cascade of extended facility shutdowns and a heatwave-driven demand spike resulted in a colossal generation void, highlighting the fragility of the energy infrastructure.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Creator",
        "fragments": [
          "why-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.78
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "A power plant component malfunction triggered a grid management action, with officials acting as emergency response architects to execute a precision load-reduction design. This intervention aimed to mitigate a massive 950-megawatt power deficit caused by a combination of a critical outage and seasonal high demand, underscoring the delicate balance of the region's power grid.",
